COMMAND NAME: mpprebuildcluster.sh

Rebuilds a Bizgres MPP master using a SQL script file containing the 
Bizgres MPP schema and MPP system catalog information, and then 
recreates all of the segment instances using the information found 
in the MPP system catalog tables.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mpprebuildcluster.sh -s <sql_file> -d <temp_db_data_directory> 
[-p <temp_db_port>] [-m] [-o] [-i] [-c <checkpoint_segments>] 
[-a] [-q] [-l <logfile_directory>]

mpprebuildcluster.sh [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mpprebuildcluster.sh script will rebuild a Bizgres MPP system using 
a SQL script file. This SQL script file must contain commands for creating 
the Bizgres MPP schema and loading system catalog data from another 
Bizgres MPP installation. There are two ways to get the SQL script file 
that mpprebuildcluster.sh needs:

* mpp_dump  The mpp_dump operation creates a file on the master 
  host called mpp_catalog_<master_id>_<timestamp>.

* pg_dump  PostgreSQL provides a utility called pg_dump, which backs 
  up a single PostgreSQL database. You can use this utility to backup the 
  template1 database of the master host, which contains the Bizgres MPP 
  schema and system catalog. For example, run the following command on 
  the MPP master host:
  pg_dump -f mpp_catalog -Fp -n mpp -a -p 5432 template1

The use of the mpprebuildcluster.sh script assumes that you have an 
existing or previous Bizgres MPP system that you want to recreate. 
By default this script uses the same hosts, ports, and data directories 
as the reference Bizgres MPP system. You can use the -o option to 
reconfigure the system to a new master host. If you want to alter any 
other information in the system configuration (such as segment hosts, data 
directory locations, or ports) use the -m option. This option will create 
the MPP master instance only. After the MPP master is created, you can 
manually edit the MPP system catalog tables to change the system 
configuration (see the Bizgres MPP Administrator Guide for the schema 
reference). After editing the system catalog tables, use the mpprebuildseg.sh 
script, which rebuilds the segment instances using the information found in 
the MPP masters system catalog tables.The use of this script also assumes 
that you have the same number of segment instances as the reference system 
you are rebuilding. If you are expanding your system or are dramatically 
changing your system configuration, you should use mppcreatecluster.sh to 
create a new Bizgres MPP system from scratch.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-s <sql_file>
Required. A SQL file containing the Bizgres MPP schema and system catalog 
information. This is the mpp_catalog_<master_id>_<timestamp> file created 
on the MPP master host by the mpp_dump operation. You can also do a 
pg_dump operation on a MPP master host to get a SQL file that can be used 
by mpprebuildcluster.sh. For example:
pg_dump -f mpp_catalog -Fp -n mpp -a -p 5432 template1

-d <temp_db_data_directory>

Required. The rebuild script creates a temporary database in this location. 
The temporary database is used to parse the contents of the SQL script file, 
and is then deleted after the rebuild operation is complete. Choose a 
different data storage location than the one used by your production MPP 
master instance.

-p <temp_db_port>

Optional. If not specified, the default port of 55555 is used. The rebuild 
script starts the temporary database using this port. The temporary database 
is used to parse the contents of the SQL script file, and is then deleted 
after the rebuild operation is complete. Choose a different port than the 
one used by your production MPP master instance.

-m

Optional. This option creates the MPP master instance only (the Bizgres MPP 
schema and system catalog), but does not create the segment instances as 
specified in the system catalog. The default behavior is to rebuild all 
segment instances as they existed when the backup file was created. Use 
this option if you want to change any information in your system 
configuration (such as segment hosts, data storage locations, or ports) 
before rebuilding the segments. After the MPP master is created, you can 
manually edit the system catalog tables to change the configuration 
(see the Bizgres MPP Administrator Guide for the MPP schema reference). 
After editing the system catalog tables, use the mpprebuildseg.sh script, 
which rebuilds the segment instances using the information found in the 
MPP masters system catalog tables.

-o

Optional. Use this option if you are rebuilding the Bizgres MPP system using 
a different master host than the one from which the backup SQL file was 
created. This option will override the master hostname found in the system 
catalog and set it to the current host name.

-i

If a backup master host is found in the system catalog configuration, 
initialize the backup master synchronization process after rebuilding 
the backup master host.

-a

Do not prompt the user for confirmation.

-q
Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.

-l logfile_directory

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/mppAdminLogs.

-?

Displays the online help.

-v

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.

*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Rebuild an entire Bizgres MPP system (master and segment instances) using the 
exact same array configuration as in the SQL backup file:

mpprebuildcluster.sh -s mpp_catalog_0_1_2005103112453 -d /home/bgadmin/tmp

Rebuild an entire Bizgres MPP system (master and segment instances) using the 
same array configuration as in the SQL backup file, but change the master host 
instance configuration to the current host:

mpprebuildcluster.sh -s mpp_catalog_0_1_2005103112453 -d /home/bgadmin/tmp -o

Rebuild the MPP master host only (the Bizgres MPP schema and system catalog):

mpprebuildcluster.sh -s mpp_catalog_0_1_2005103112453 -d /home/bgadmin/tmp -o -m


